(7311765, 1140057, 86218, '<td valign="top">From the Critique club<br/> <br/>Good improvising and the warm son contrasted by the cold place does work well. You can almost imagine yourself wanting to stand in this light - but not familiar with this kind of conditions Im sure the sunshine is deceptive as even with this it can be very cold.<br/>Comp looks good and nice lead in to image with enough interest on sides to bring eye back as well as clouds naturally bringing the eye down again.<br/> <br/>Notes on processing I suppose is a personal thing and I cant say Im a big fan of this kind of processing where you loose allot of the natural feel of the beautiful setting. I note another comment also not liking the clouds but even lower down the whites in the water is so unnatural that you wonder if it''s not some artificial plastic in it. i might have opted for a slightly warmer tone to this as it could help in the theme of the challenge. <br/> <br/>Nice finish and many people hope to get a 6 in any challenge.</td>', 'From the Critique club Good improvising and the warm son contrasted by the cold place does work well. You can almost imagine yourself wanting to stand in this light - but not familiar with this kind of conditions Im sure the sunshine is deceptive as even with this it can be very cold.Comp looks good and nice lead in to image with enough interest on sides to bring eye back as well as clouds naturally bringing the eye down again. Notes on processing I suppose is a personal thing and I cant say Im a big fan of this kind of processing where you loose allot of the natural feel of the beautiful setting. I note another comment also not liking the clouds but even lower down the whites in the water is so unnatural that you wonder if it''s not some artificial plastic in it. i might have opted for a slightly warmer tone to this as it could help in the theme of the challenge.  Nice finish and many people hope to get a 6 in any challenge.', '2015-02-05 07:38:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(7397424, 1139804, 25024, '<td valign="top">I would have liked to have this critiqued by another member but alas, it was not to be...</td>', 'I would have liked to have this critiqued by another member but alas, it was not to be...', '2015-08-14 12:51:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(7397427, 1140081, 25024, '<td valign="top">*Hello from Sid and the Critique Club*<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge well.<br/> <br/>What I like most about your image is the crop it makes the image very appealing and so much more interesting than the bog standard ''chuck it in the middle'' approach that is so often seen. However, what lets it down badly is what I suspect to be camera shake. I''m not sure what size your lens was but as you are probably already aware your shutter speed needs to be correspondingly higher as you go further up the telephoto range. There is no sharpness anywhere which has also been exacerbated by your cropping in on it, perhaps at original resolution you may have got away with it, but it is plainly evident here I''m afraid.<br/> <br/>It is essential to meet this challenge that you caught the flame in a very obvious sort of way and this you have achieved, well done. The sky is a very vivid blue I think it would benefit from being toned a little, it is quite overpowering as it is.<br/> <br/>It''s a shame that it wasn''t sharper it would have scored higher but thanks for submitting, Sid.</td>', '*Hello from Sid and the Critique Club* An appealing image that meets the challenge well. What I like most about your image is the crop it makes the image very appealing and so much more interesting than the bog standard ''chuck it in the middle'' approach that is so often seen. However, what lets it down badly is what I suspect to be camera shake. I''m not sure what size your lens was but as you are probably already aware your shutter speed needs to be correspondingly higher as you go further up the telephoto range. There is no sharpness anywhere which has also been exacerbated by your cropping in on it, perhaps at original resolution you may have got away with it, but it is plainly evident here I''m afraid. It is essential to meet this challenge that you caught the flame in a very obvious sort of way and this you have achieved, well done. The sky is a very vivid blue I think it would benefit from being toned a little, it is quite overpowering as it is. It''s a shame that it wasn''t sharper it would have scored higher but thanks for submitting, Sid.', '2015-08-14 13:04:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(7402907, 1139804, 50695, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 6. One positive thing I''m noticing now is how freakishly big the shadow of the lantern top is. Adds a lot of interest to the shot.</td>', 'I gave this a 6. One positive thing I''m noticing now is how freakishly big the shadow of the lantern top is. Adds a lot of interest to the shot.', '2015-09-07 00:29:12.000000', NULL, 0),
